app/init/launch.ts:290-294 — and the returned route is the tab group:

  290|    logInfo('Route app to Home screen');
  291|    return {
  292|        route: '/(authenticated)/(home)',

-- There is no town hall / first-channel fallback anywhere in the launch path: with nothing saved,
-- the app lands on the channel list with its tab bar.

detox/maestro/flows/account/attach_logs.yml:61-83 (v2.45.0) — upstream's own flow depends on that:
after `launchApp stopApp: true, clearState: false` it waits for `tab_bar.home.tab` and the comment
says the relaunch "lands on the Home tab".


== [4] What our app measured (T39-R2), for comparison

docs/t39-r2-build-note.md §4.1 and §6 F-1; docs/t39-r2-evidence-2026-10-27.log §6:
a launch that had pushed Town Square answered a `nativeChannelPane` under a NavigationBar holding
`Back`, and no `TabBar` node at all; a launch that had not pushed answered
`Home / Threads / Search / Mentions / Saved`.

-- That is upstream's phone behaviour, not a defect: a channel is a pushed screen and the tab bar is
-- gone until the reader goes Back. What was wrong was the test's assumption that the bar is always
-- on screen (and, separately, that a launch with nothing saved opens the town hall — see [3]).

